# Handling Protocols

> How to handle every situation that isn't "write the next line." When in doubt, follow the protocol; the protocol beats improvisation.

---

## 1. File & folder handling

**Naming (all lowercase, no spaces, no surprises):**
- Folders & non-component files: **kebab-case** — `media-session.ts`, `handling-protocols.md`, `upload-queue/`.
- React components & their files: **PascalCase** — `RadioPlayer.tsx`, `MemoRecorder.tsx`. One component per file; file name = component name.
- Hooks: `useX.ts` camelCase — `useMediaSession.ts`.
- Tests: mirror the subject — `RadioPlayer.test.tsx`, `upload-queue.test.ts`; visual/e2e in `tests/visual/*.spec.ts`.
- Types/schemas: `*.types.ts`, `*.schema.ts`.
- Env: `.env.local` (never committed), `.env.example` (committed, keys only, no values).
- Docs: kebab-case `.md` in `docs/`.

**Placement rules:**
- Code lives in exactly one place. A helper used by 2+ packages moves to `packages/shared`; a UI primitive used by 2+ apps moves to `packages/ui`. Do not copy — hoist.
- Anything ephemeral (scratch, screenshots, logs, downloads) goes in `.scratch/` (git-ignored), **never** in source dirs. The macOS scratchpad wipes between sessions — anything durable belongs in the repo and pushed.
- Generated files (`.next/`, `node_modules/`, `dist/`, coverage) are git-ignored, never committed.
- A folder gets an `index.ts` barrel only when it has a stable public surface used elsewhere; do not barrel private internals (it bloats bundles — see perf law).

**Labeling:** every non-obvious module starts with a one-line comment stating its job. Deliberate shortcuts carry a `ponytail:` comment naming the ceiling and the upgrade path.

**Directories are created just-in-time** for the slice that needs them. Never scaffold empty folders "for later."

