## 5. Sandbox test protocol

Runs in isolation before any PR merges. **Nothing here touches `prod` or live data.**

Order (fail fast — stop at first red, fix, restart):
1. `pnpm typecheck` — TypeScript, zero errors.
2. `pnpm lint` — ESLint + a11y lint (`eslint-plugin-jsx-a11y`), zero errors.
3. `pnpm test` — unit/integration (Vitest). Non-trivial logic must have a test; audio state machine, upload queue, and any crypto path are mandatory-tested.
4. `pnpm build` — production build succeeds; inspect the route bundle sizes against the perf law (≤170KB gz/route).
5. **Performance gates** — Lighthouse CI (mobile preset) against the built app; assert the budgets in `implementation.md` §1. Any regression = red.

Run against a **throwaway dev server / clean build dir**, seeded with fixture data, never the real backend. Secrets come from `.env.local`; the sandbox uses `.env.test` fixtures.

A PR is not "green" until 1–5 all pass **and** the visual test (§6) passes.

